!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/valid/a-refined-constructor-applied-is-an-entry-apart-from-the-sugar-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.3, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.7, [TSON-SCHEMA] §8.2"
  description: """
    The fixture's `rows` refines `meta.array`, pinning `min_items`: a refined constructor, a named kind of array as the
    kernel's `set_type` is. `rows<uuid>` is construction sugar, `!rows { element_type: uuid }`, a content-keyed
    synthetic built with `rows`; `[uuid; 1..]` is `!meta.array { element_type: uuid  min_items: 1 }`, built with
    `array`. They admit the same data and are two entries, neither IS-A the other, since identity is the binding record
    and its constructor. Neither records an application: a construction substitutes nothing.
    """
  valid: {
    resolved: """
      !schema {
        post => !meta.record { fields: {
          a => !meta.record_field { type: rows_uuid_xxhash }
          b => !meta.record_field { type: array_uuid_1_xxhash }
        } }

        @meta.synthetic rows_uuid_xxhash => !rows { element_type: uuid }

        @meta.synthetic array_uuid_1_xxhash => !meta.array { element_type: uuid  min_items: 1 }
      }
      """
  }
}
